00:32:41.140 --> 00:32:43.920
I didn't particularly like enemy placement.

00:32:44.240 --> 00:32:45.940
I think there was a lot of stuff.

00:32:46.160 --> 00:32:53.200
I think it also has this thing, and it's not entirely true when you're Little Nemo because

00:32:53.200 --> 00:33:00.380
you're, like, normal platformer protagonist-sized when you're Little Nemo.

00:33:00.440 --> 00:33:03.980
But when you are an animal, you are massive on that screen.

00:33:04.200 --> 00:33:07.160
And it just... And these enemies are usually massive.

00:33:07.420 --> 00:33:12.540
So there's just so many opportunities to just get in places where you cannot avoid getting

00:33:12.540 --> 00:33:21.020
hit. And I think that's where a lot of my frustration was when we were talking about hardness and

00:33:21.020 --> 00:33:23.940
difficulty. Like, I think that's where I was getting it.

00:33:24.300 --> 00:33:32.840
I think if, like, maybe everything was sort of the standard, you know, platform protagonist

00:33:32.840 --> 00:33:34.560
size would be a little less that.

00:33:34.560 --> 00:33:35.840
But maybe that's the point, too.

00:33:35.980 --> 00:33:42.420
Like, if you're an animal, you've got maneuverability perks, and it's just trying to balance that

00:33:42.420 --> 00:33:45.020
out. But yeah, it was frustrating.

00:33:46.420 --> 00:33:50.740
Yeah, I mean, I won't pretend that I didn't have times where I was frustrated or that I,

00:33:51.080 --> 00:33:54.080
