00:38:43.920 --> 00:38:46.580
It's the same thing, you know,

00:38:46.700 --> 00:38:50.460
with most games up until, basically,

00:38:50.800 --> 00:38:52.300
video games started becoming movies,

00:38:52.300 --> 00:38:54.920
where now all of a sudden it's like, you know,

00:38:55.600 --> 00:38:58.120
should I be excited if I beat God of War?

00:38:58.320 --> 00:38:59.660
Like, not really, right?

00:38:59.820 --> 00:39:02.040
Like, they plan for everybody to beat that game,

00:39:02.080 --> 00:39:04.300
and they make it so that anybody can beat that game.

00:39:04.440 --> 00:39:06.640
I'm not saying, like, a four-year-old kid

00:39:06.640 --> 00:39:10.040
could beat that game, but, like, video games are a lot less challenging today

00:39:10.040 --> 00:39:11.220
than they were,

00:39:11.460 --> 00:39:13.280
and I know that that's not a hot take.

00:39:13.400 --> 00:39:14.320
I'm just saying that part

00:39:14.320 --> 00:39:16.220
to get to the next part about Lil' Nemo,

00:39:16.340 --> 00:39:18.600
which is, because we're so good

00:39:18.600 --> 00:39:21.260
