00:45:38.600 --> 00:45:42.740
But I don't think I'm gonna put this one on the Essential Games list.

00:45:42.780 --> 00:45:51.660
If only because I did feel rather limited in what the gameplay loop was.

00:45:51.660 --> 00:45:54.900
I didn't enjoy particularly collecting the keys in the stage.

00:45:54.920 --> 00:45:56.540
It wasn't enjoyable to backtrack.

00:45:56.540 --> 00:46:03.960
It would have been interesting if they could have found a way to just make it so that the keys that you collect in the stage aren't just used at the end of the stage,

00:46:04.100 --> 00:46:12.620
but rather to, in like Legend of Zelda style, like use those keys to unlock other areas to then get like the next key.

00:46:12.900 --> 00:46:16.120
But the order that you go, like any key could have opened any door.

00:46:16.120 --> 00:46:26.820
So technically you could just continue to go in your own way, but you ultimately have to explore the entire area the first time through rather than the backtracking.

00:46:27.380 --> 00:46:31.200
The animals are a fun part of the game.

00:46:31.320 --> 00:46:33.420
And I think it's pretty neat that there's so many of them.

00:46:33.660 --> 00:46:35.460
I mean, I'm not quite even sure.

00:46:35.460 --> 00:46:45.060
Like that's pretty cool for like in terms of a power-up system, like just having this many unique ways to explore the platforming levels.

00:46:45.340 --> 00:46:51.720
But they're also like kind of limited in their like usefulness.

00:46:51.720 --> 00:46:54.800
Like it's very clear which ones you should be using.

00:46:54.800 --> 00:47:06.340
And I don't think there was really a moment to be like in future Kirby games, there are animals as well that like Kirby can hop on like a hamster, an owl.

00:47:07.960 --> 00:47:08.920
These are great.

00:47:09.580 --> 00:47:16.460
A frog. These are great things for Kirby, but they're also like, oh, and I want to stick with this guy for the next level, right?

00:47:16.580 --> 00:47:19.620
Because technically like you could use the owl in any level.

00:47:20.040 --> 00:47:22.780
You don't get that same ability here with these animals.

00:47:22.780 --> 00:47:25.280
They are like short little bursts.

00:47:25.580 --> 00:47:36.140
And I think it would have been more interesting to like have a system where you kind of could be any of the animals, but it's more about what strengths and weaknesses you want to impose on yourself.

00:47:36.760 --> 00:47:40.600
So I'm not going to put it on the essential games list, but I do think it's a pretty darn good game.

00:47:40.960 --> 00:47:44.680
And like I said, while it may be challenging, I don't view it as impossible.

00:47:45.180 --> 00:47:49.520
Joe. Another week here where I kind of went through a little bit of a roller coaster.

00:47:49.740 --> 00:47:51.060
I know we did the same thing last week.

00:47:51.060 --> 00:47:55.740
But yeah, I started out lukewarm on this game.

00:47:55.960 --> 00:48:08.440
But as I played it more, I'll say that one of my favorite things about Super Mario Brothers 3 is getting the Tanooki suit or getting the frog suit or, you know, and seeing what these new powers do.

00:48:08.500 --> 00:48:11.700
And that only happens like twice, you know, because those are rare suits.

00:48:11.800 --> 00:48:12.920
You get there's only a couple of them.

00:48:12.920 --> 00:48:22.120
This is like getting the Tanooki suit the game where there's all these different suits or animal power ups.

00:48:22.120 --> 00:48:32.720
And I really did enjoy like that twist on the platformer where it's like, hey, if you want to be able to climb up this thing, you need this animal.

00:48:32.920 --> 00:48:34.080
And like, hey, what does this animal do?

00:48:34.740 --> 00:48:36.460
It lets you dig below the ground.

00:48:36.460 --> 00:48:40.220
And this one lets you hover for, you know, a few paces.

00:48:40.520 --> 00:48:44.600
And I like that part of it a lot.

00:48:44.600 --> 00:48:48.340
I also just found this game very clean and charming.

00:48:48.720 --> 00:48:58.000
I mean, I think that like what was holding me back from voting in on the essential games list was like, is there enough going on?

00:48:58.180 --> 00:49:00.740
But, you know, like, does it change enough?

00:49:00.880 --> 00:49:13.800
But the more I think about it, the more I don't think it has to change enough because it's the change and the refresh of it all comes from finding these new animal things and dealing with new enemies using these different animals in different ways.

00:49:13.800 --> 00:49:16.020
I don't know. I just think it's a really cool gameplay loop.

00:49:16.160 --> 00:49:17.020
I really like the music.

00:49:17.500 --> 00:49:19.440
I think I'm going to vote it on the essential games list.

00:49:20.400 --> 00:49:23.080
Sean. All right.

00:49:23.420 --> 00:49:33.600
So as the one here that has not seen the movie or read the 19, the turn of the century comic strip.

00:49:35.540 --> 00:49:46.320
I was super into the animal transformation slash mounting concept in this game.

00:49:46.400 --> 00:49:48.160
I thought it was really interesting.

00:49:48.820 --> 00:49:54.820
And now while recording this episode, I'm learning that that's not even like a little Nemo thing.

00:49:55.240 --> 00:49:58.180
Like that's not even a part of it.

00:49:58.180 --> 00:49:59.020
It's not a thing he does.

00:49:59.180 --> 00:50:00.500
It's not a thing that he does.

00:50:00.500 --> 00:50:04.780
So now I'm just confused and and and that's kind of like.

00:50:05.580 --> 00:50:08.860
I'm just confused about what this game is supposed to be doing.

00:50:12.040 --> 00:50:17.020
Now, that being said, like all the complaints that I have are valid like that.

00:50:17.240 --> 00:50:18.140
Not not sorry.

00:50:18.440 --> 00:50:19.260
They're not valid.

00:50:19.440 --> 00:50:28.340
They still hold water in my eyes in terms of just the idea that a lot of these things I really enjoy.

00:50:29.220 --> 00:50:30.260
On paper.

00:50:30.640 --> 00:50:34.380
And I thought were cool as I was discovering them.

00:50:35.580 --> 00:50:41.160
And then just kind of got annoyed with as the game went on.

00:50:41.400 --> 00:50:44.560
Like sort of how Joe was saying he started off lukewarm.

00:50:44.680 --> 00:50:46.020
I kind of stayed lukewarm.

00:50:46.840 --> 00:50:52.760
I'm not going to say that this game is not pretty and is does not have variety.

00:50:53.080 --> 00:50:56.220
But I think that a lot of the concepts are a little half baked.

00:50:56.540 --> 00:51:03.100
I think that a lot of the animals should have had like some other things to them.

00:51:03.280 --> 00:51:05.900
Aside from just like movement speed and jump height.

00:51:13.160 --> 00:51:17.960
I can't put it on the essential games list in terms of just my opinion of the game.

00:51:18.960 --> 00:51:22.900
But I do think that there is a lot of value in playing the game.

00:51:23.120 --> 00:51:25.500
It is cool. I just don't think it's essential.

00:51:26.080 --> 00:51:31.760
Fair enough. I also I did mean to say that I do not think this is an essential adaptation of Little Nemo.

00:51:31.760 --> 00:51:34.480
Because I don't know where it has to stuff.

00:51:34.480 --> 00:51:36.000
Yeah no that wasn't a part of it.

00:51:36.140 --> 00:51:37.020
But the game itself.

00:51:37.400 --> 00:51:38.860
That wasn't the basis.

00:51:39.800 --> 00:51:41.240
But it was still confusing.

00:51:42.980 --> 00:51:46.260
I personally would just like to see more from Little Nemo.

00:51:47.300 --> 00:51:49.080
And how I don't know.

00:51:49.300 --> 00:51:51.540
Because I don't think the movie needs a sequel.

00:51:51.860 --> 00:51:52.720
Or a remake.

00:51:53.900 --> 00:51:55.340
And I don't know.

00:51:55.480 --> 00:51:57.740
Maybe I just want that JRPG game and that's it.

00:51:57.880 --> 00:51:59.040
Maybe that's enough for me.

00:51:59.040 --> 00:52:03.600
Maybe I want a game where you finally see his pet flying squirrel.

00:52:04.080 --> 00:52:06.480
Maybe I want a game where you have to have.

00:52:07.160 --> 00:52:12.260
You have to use the GameCube microphone to say the pajama pajama spell.

00:52:12.480 --> 00:52:14.440
In order to take care of the Nightmare King.

